A||||3||Pheagey||Cleaning the Throttlebody on and '88 coupe||||1||
Z||000000||Pheagey||10-08-2001||07:30 AM||||I was struck with the idea of cleaning my throttle body. Question is: what kinda of improvment (if any) would be gained outside of knowing I did it.<BR>Thanks. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-08-2001||08:58 PM||||unless the thing is covered in crap probably nothing will change.... The 700TBI is one of the most rock solid fuel systems there is.<P>The most cleaning they ever really need is a shot of Gumout EFI cleaner thru each vacuum port Maybe once in a great while pop out the IAC and give that passage a shot.<P>Keep in mind that TBI isn't prone to the injector fouling that cronicly plagues port EFI.<P><BR>If you want insurance against leaks and things get the "rebuild" kit for it. this will allow you to replace all the O rings and gaskets. It also contians a new fuel regulator diaphragm and injector screens.<P>You'll also want a copy of the Haynes 86-96 fuel injection book (#10220) It covers the the 700TBI and a bunch of others. Very good read on EFI in general.<P>One other thing to check... the MAT sensor in the manifold to the right of the TBI. you can read about that in the DIS notes in my cave. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||10-09-2001||03:49 AM||||When i do mine, i take my tb off, and the intake, and use carb clean and get all the carbon off.  <P>The car idles better, and when the carbon is really bad, you can feel the car is a bit more responsive when you cleaned it out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pheagey||10-09-2001||09:41 AM||||Thanks ppl.||||reg||14
